        "thread_id": "TH1",
        "thread_goal": "Align on current move process and main problems to fix",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M1",
            "speaker_id": 77364,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Hi team, welcome to the channel for the new warehouse efficiency project. To get started on T1, can everyone share their thoughts on how we currently do moves and loading? What are the main problems you see on the floor?",
            "mentions": [
              36844,
              54508,
              81581,
              205041
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T1"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M2",
            "speaker_id": 81581,
            "reply_to": "M1",
            "text": "Good start. From my perspective, the biggest issues are: 1) No consistent stacking method between shifts, which is a safety risk. 2) Delays waiting for a forklift because nobody staged it beforehand. 3) Unclear handoff between the factory hands prepping the load and the movers who load it. We waste a lot of time just clarifying what's what.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "heavy_check_mark",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M3",
            "speaker_id": 205041,
            "reply_to": "M2",
            "text": "Yeah, the forklift thing is a big one. Sometimes we also don't have the right straps or corner protectors ready.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M4",
            "speaker_id": 77364,
            "reply_to": "M2",
            "text": "Thanks for that. So stacking, forklifts, and communication. That sounds right.",
            "mentions": [
              81581
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M5",
            "speaker_id": 36844,
            "reply_to": "M2",
            "text": "I agree with all those points. The loading sequence is different depending on who is on shift. Some people load heavy to light front to back, others do it side to side. It makes securing the load tricky.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M6",
            "speaker_id": 81581,
            "reply_to": "M5",
            "text": "Exactly. That's a perfect example of the first point. We need one standard way. It's not just about efficiency, it's about preventing load shifts during transit.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "point_up",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M7",
            "speaker_id": 54508,
            "reply_to": "M2",
            "text": "Confirming the handoff issue. Sometimes the paperwork says one thing but the pallets on the floor are different. We spend time trying to match them up.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M8",
            "speaker_id": 77364,
            "reply_to": "M7",
            "text": "Is the paperwork often wrong?",
            "mentions": [
              54508
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M9",
            "speaker_id": 81581,
            "reply_to": "M8",
            "text": "It's less about the paperwork being wrong and more about the physical prep not matching the plan. The process is disconnected. This is something we should track in the incident log A3 once we have it.",
            "mentions": [
              77364
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A3"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M10",
            "speaker_id": 81581,
            "reply_to": "M9",
            "text": "So, to summarize and move forward, let's agree on the top three problems to solve. I propose: 1. Inconsistent/unsafe loading and stacking methods. 2. Delays from poor equipment and cargo staging. 3. Unclear roles and handoffs between crews. Does everyone agree with this focus?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D1"
            ],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M11",
